{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.PairwiseCumulantVanishing","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.tripleMutual_neg_of_b3_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.tripleMutual_neg_of_b3_pos","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L238-L246","doc":"**A positive 3-body cumulant forces the Brunnian triple channel to be negative.** With the\npair terms gone, `b₃ = −(triple mutual energy)` exactly, so the sign of the measured cumulant\nfixes the sign of the channel with nothing in between. AME gives `b₃ > 0`, hence an attractive\n(negative-energy) three-body mutual channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.pairLocal_of_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.pairLocal_of_constant","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L222-L226","doc":"**Non-vacuity of `PairLocal`.** A model whose pair weight is literally the same function in\nevery cluster size is pair-local, so `isPairwise_of_pairLocal` is not vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.b3_eq_neg_tripleMutual_of_noIsolatedPairEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.b3_eq_neg_tripleMutual_of_noIsolatedPairEnergy","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L212-L220","doc":"**With a Brunnian carrier the 3-body cumulant is exactly the negated triple mutual energy.**\nNo pair contamination and no free constant: the pair terms vanish identically, so the whole of\n`b₃` is the irreducibly three-body channel. Measuring `b₃` therefore pins that channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.not_pairLocal_of_noIsolatedPairEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.not_pairLocal_of_noIsolatedPairEnergy","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L203-L210","doc":"**A Brunnian carrier violates pair-locality**, provided some triple is nontrivial — which is\nthe defining content of Brunnian-ness, that the whole is linked while every pair is not. So the\nBrunnian property is not incidental: it is what lets `binding = −(mutual energy)` coexist with a\nnonzero measured 3-body cumulant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.not_pairLocal_of_b3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.not_pairLocal_of_b3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L193-L199","doc":"**The load-bearing direction: a nonzero 3-body cumulant refutes pair-locality.** AME2020\nmeasures `b₃ = +1.4262225` (`QOU.MassTheory.AmeBindingNotPairwise.ame_b3_eq`), so the crossing\nstructure between two components *must* depend on what else is present. This is a constraint on\nthe carrier derived from data, not a modelling choice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.b4_eq_zero_of_pairLocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.b4_eq_zero_of_pairLocal","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L188-L191","doc":"**And the 4-body cumulant too.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.b3_eq_zero_of_pairLocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.b3_eq_zero_of_pairLocal","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L182-L186","doc":"**So a pair-local crossing model has identically vanishing 3-body cumulant.** Composing with\n`PairwiseCumulantVanishing.b3_eq_zero_of_isPairwise`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.isPairwise_of_pairLocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.isPairwise_of_pairLocal","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L167-L180","doc":"**Pair-locality makes the crossing model pairwise-additive.** Grouping the mutual energy by\npair is automatic; it is assembly-independence of the pair weights that produces the shape\n`PairwiseCumulantVanishing.IsPairwise`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.toBindingMap_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.toBindingMap_quad","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L161-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.toBindingMap_triple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.toBindingMap_triple","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L158-L159","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.toBindingMap_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.toBindingMap_pair","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L155-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.toBindingMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.toBindingMap","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L147-L153","doc":"The binding map induced by the crossing model, via\n`SelfMutualPartition.binding_eq_neg_mutualEnergy`: each cluster's binding is the negative of its\nmutual energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.quadMutual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.quadMutual","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L142-L145","doc":"The total mutual energy of the four-component assembly: its six pairs, each measured inside\nthe assembly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.tripleMutual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.tripleMutual","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L138-L140","doc":"The total mutual energy of the triple `{i,j,k}`: its three pairs, each measured inside the\ntriple. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.NoIsolatedPairEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.NoIsolatedPairEnergy","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L118-L136","doc":"**`NoIsolatedPairEnergy`** (RENAMED 2026-09-07 from `Brunnian`): a crossing model in which\na pair measured in\nisolation carries no mutual energy.\n\n**CORRECTED 2026-09-07 — this docstring cited `QOU.Mass.BrunnianBindingChannel` as\nestablishing that the ³He/⁴He carrier `L6a4` \"has this property\". It does not; it proves\nthe opposite.** That file establishes L6a4 has vanishing pairwise *Gauss linking number*\n(`n₊ = n₋`) and then proves `brunnian_binding_survives`: the mutual energy of such a pair\nis **strictly positive**, `0 < countChannel m m q` for `0 < m`, `1 < q`. Its whole point\nis that binding *survives* the Brunnian vanishing.\n\nSo two distinct properties share one name — topological (linking number zero, TRUE of\nL6a4) and energetic (`w₂ = 0`, FALSE of it) — and the first does not imply the second.\nConsequently `b3_eq_neg_tripleMutual_of_brunnian` below is a correct theorem whose\nhypothesis **L6a4 does not satisfy**, and the measured `b₃` does not cleanly pin the\ntriple channel. Independently, the measured `b₂ = 2.2245662` MeV refutes this hypothesis\noutright. Both refutations are formalised, sorry-free, in\n`QOU.Mass.BrunnianHypothesisNotSatisfied`.  Tier table for the four things this corpus calls `Brunnian`, and which implications hold: `QOU.Mass.BrunnianTierDisambiguation`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.PairLocal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.PairLocal","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L112-L116","doc":"**Pair-locality**: a pair's mutual energy does not depend on what else is in the assembly.\nThis is the hypothesis that turns `binding = −(mutual energy)` into a pairwise-additive binding,\nand the one the measured 3-body cumulant refutes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.w4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.w4","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L106-L106","doc":"mutual energy of the pair `{i,j}` measured inside the four-component assembly ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.w3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.w3","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L104-L104","doc":"mutual energy of the pair `{i,j}` measured inside the triple `{i,j,k}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.w2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.w2","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L102-L102","doc":"mutual energy of the pair `{i,j}` measured in the isolated pair ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.CrossingModelPairLocality.CrossingModel","kind":"structure","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/CrossingModelPairLocality.lean#L92-L106","doc":"The inter-component crossing energy of a four-component assembly, **grouped by the pair each\ncrossing joins**. Every crossing joins exactly two components, so this grouping is a bookkeeping\nidentity rather than an assumption; what is *not* assumed is that a pair's weight is the same\nacross cluster sizes, which is why there are three fields rather than one.\n\n* `w2 i j` — the mutual energy of the pair `{i,j}` in the isolated two-component assembly;\n* `w3 i j k` — the mutual energy of the pair `{i,j}` inside the triple `{i,j,k}`;\n* `w4 i j` — the mutual energy of the pair `{i,j}` inside the full four-component assembly. ","signatureChunk":0}]}